      "math_academy_id": "q-83223",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "$$\n(P∨Q)⇔Q\\,≡\\,\\bbox[3pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAAAAAAA}}∧[Q⇒(P∨Q)]\n$$\n\nWhat expression should be inserted into the blank space above to give logically equivalent statements?",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nSo in this case, we have\n\n$$\n(P∨Q)⇔Q≡[\\,(P∨Q)⇒Q]∧[Q⇒(P∨Q)].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is $(P∨Q)⇒Q.$",
